message.content:
{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together district and taluka level plantation status information for the Maharashtra Forest Department, focused on the “10 crore” plantation initiative. It supports monitoring of progress across administrative units and can be used for planning, review, and performance tracking by forest and forestry stakeholders. The coverage is for Maharashtra, as indicated in the catalog title, with the latest referenced edition being 2025.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers the 12th Five Year Plan for Prasar Bharati, focusing on ongoing schemes and new initiatives across broadcasting infrastructure, content development and dissemination, and special projects. It supports planning and monitoring of programme-wise activities under the Ministry of Information and Broadcasting. The scope is limited to Delhi, reflecting the location context for the plan’s implementation and related scheme activities.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Broadcasting; Broadcasting"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The 6th Minor Irrigation Census Data catalog compiles borewell-related information for minor irrigation purposes, supporting assessment of groundwater-based irrigation infrastructure. It helps planners and researchers understand the extent and characteristics of borewell usage for irrigation and use the findings for monitoring, policy formulation, and resource planning. The focus is on groundwater-linked minor irrigation assets, enabling analysis at the level of irrigation purpose borewell details.",
  "generated_sector": "Water Resources; Ground Water"
}

{
  "generated_description": "AAI policy focuses on enabling women’s entrepreneurship and leadership in the tourism sector. It aims to empower women in the state by supporting initiatives that strengthen participation and capability within tourism-related activities. The policy is oriented toward fostering local leadership and business development opportunities for women, with an emphasis on tourism as a driver of inclusive growth.",
  "generated_sector": "Travel and Tourism; Places"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers Andhra Pradesh’s public grievance redressal and monitoring mechanism that supports a reformed, centralized workflow across government departments. It is implemented through an application that enables grievance initiation, tracking, and oversight by heads of departments, integrating multiple departments into a unified digital process. The system supports re-engineering and digital transformation for grievance handling, helping improve responsiveness and accountability in public service delivery.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Grievances"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides RBK-wise procurement details for APMARKFED in Andhra Pradesh, supporting analysis of procurement flows and sourcing patterns. It is useful for monitoring supply and procurement performance, planning and review of agricultural procurement operations, and transparency-oriented reporting. The focus is on procurement quantities and related details organized by RBK, enabling comparisons across procurement centers within the state.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Agricultural Produces"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Season wise procurement details for commodities handled through APMARKFED in Andhra Pradesh, capturing how procurement varies across seasons. The catalog supports analysis of seasonal trends in buying, planning of procurement operations, and monitoring of commodity flows for stakeholders. It is useful for researchers and administrators looking to understand seasonality in agricultural procurement and its implications for supply planning. The data is published under the Agriculture domain.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Agricultural Produces"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Year-wise records of ASIDE scheme funds provided by the Government of India to Madhya Pradesh focus on infrastructure development of exports. The catalog covers assistance details such as the number of projects (pariyojana), total sanctioned cost, amounts received from GoI, and disbursement to running units. It supports tracking fund flows and monitoring project-level financial progress for export infrastructure initiatives in Madhya Pradesh.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Manufacturing"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles assets managed by the Karnataka Forest Department, covering departmental nurseries, plantations, and forests. It brings together information on key forest-related holdings such as nursery and plantation areas and the extent of forests under departmental management. These records support planning, monitoring, and reporting for forestry operations, including development and maintenance of forest assets. The scope is Karnataka, as indicated in the catalog title.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The AYUSH Beneficiaries catalog covers outpatient (OPD) services for Ayurveda, Unani, Homeopathy and Yoga and Nature cure, focusing on beneficiary-related information. It supports monitoring and planning of AYUSH service delivery and utilization within Karnataka. The collection is aligned with family welfare and health service needs, enabling stakeholders to assess OPD coverage and inform program improvements at the state level.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Family Welfare"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers AYUSH educational institutions in Karnataka, including government and private colleges offering Ayurveda, Unani, Homeopathy, and Yoga and Nature cure. It supports users seeking information on training and academic availability across these traditional and complementary medicine streams. The focus is on educational institutions that enable study and professional preparation in AYUSH disciplines within the state.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The AYUSH Services catalog covers availability and service delivery of AYUSH facilities in Karnataka, including AYUSH hospitals, dispensaries, collocated PHCs, AYUSH wings, Panchakarma units, and AYUSH health and wellness centers. It also includes service models such as dispensaries in PPP mode and upgraded hospitals under NAM, along with government central pharmacy, AYUSH research and training centers. The catalog supports planning, monitoring, and assessment of AYUSH healthcare infrastructure and related capacity-building activities.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Monthly Aadhaar enrolment and update data are compiled across India, with breakdowns by age group and by pin code. The catalog supports monitoring of identity coverage and service uptake over time, enabling analysis of enrolment trends and update activity for policy planning and program evaluation. It is published under the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY) and the Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI), and is useful for researchers and administrators tracking demographic and geographic patterns in Aadhaar lifecycle events.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Union/State Government Administration"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides district-wise Aadhaar seeding status of eligible households covered under the National Food Security Act (NFSA), 2013 for Madhya Pradesh. It covers Aadhaar-linked households and eligible population under the Public Distribution System (PDS), including counts of families and persons with Aadhaar numbers and their corresponding seeding percentages against totals. The information supports monitoring of UIDAI-linked beneficiary coverage and helps assess progress in Aadhaar seeding for NFSA entitlements across districts.",
  "generated_sector": "Food; Public Distribution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on Aaple Sarkar Seva Kendra in Beed District, supporting access to public services through a local service-delivery model. It is intended to help citizens and stakeholders understand and use the service center’s offerings and related information for smoother governance interactions. The scope covers Beed District in Maharashtra, enabling district-level use cases such as service guidance and citizen facilitation. The catalog is organized around the Aaple Sarkar Seva Kendra initiative.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Local Government"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides district-wise abstract details related to revenue released and cashew plantation activities in Karnataka. It supports analysis of territorial performance by linking revenue release information with cashew plantation coverage at the district level. These records are useful for planning, monitoring, and evaluating agricultural produce initiatives and resource allocation for cashew cultivation. The focus on revenue and plantation indicators helps stakeholders assess trends and district-level outcomes over time.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Agricultural Produces"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides district-level abstracts of the area under food crops in Tamil Nadu for 2016-17. It supports analysis of crop area distribution across districts, helping planners and researchers understand regional patterns in food crop cultivation. The focus on food crop area makes it useful for agricultural monitoring, policy formulation, and evidence-based planning at the district level within Tamil Nadu.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Crops"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides district-level statistics on the total area under food crops and non-food crops in Tamil Nadu for 2016-17. It supports analysis of agricultural land use patterns across districts, helping researchers and planners compare crop area distribution between food and non-food categories. The data can be used for monitoring agricultural trends, informing policy and resource allocation, and supporting reporting and decision-making by relevant government stakeholders.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Crops"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together academic programmes offered through the Tamil Virtual Academy (TVA) in Tamil Nadu. It supports learners, educators, and institutions in discovering programme options and planning enrolment or collaborations. The focus is on programme-level information under the TVA department, aligned with information and technology initiatives in education. Use cases include programme awareness, academic planning, and reference for stakeholders seeking TVA offerings within Tamil Nadu.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Information and Technology"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles accident statistics for Punjab, focusing on how the number of accidents varies by the class of vehicle involved. It covers multiple vehicle categories such as two wheelers, auto-rickshaw, car, jeep, bus, truck, tractor, tempo, station wagons, and tractor with trailors, along with other vehicle classes. These data support transport safety analysis, risk profiling by vehicle type, and planning targeted interventions for road safety in Punjab.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles statistics on accidents in factories of Punjab, covering the number of workers employed alongside fatal and non-fatal accident counts. It supports analysis of workplace safety trends and risk patterns for industrial settings, enabling comparisons over time and across accident severity. These data are useful for labour and safety monitoring, policy planning, and targeted interventions to reduce factory accidents in Punjab.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Unorganized Sector Workers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers information on active job card holders under MGNREGS in Karnataka. It supports monitoring of rural employment demand and participation through job card–based tracking, useful for program management, planning, and performance review by rural development and Panchayati Raj stakeholders. The focus is on active beneficiaries holding MGNREGS job cards, enabling analysis of coverage and outreach at the state level.",
  "generated_sector": "Rural; Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles information on active workers engaged under MGNREGS in Karnataka, supporting monitoring of rural employment generation and workforce participation. It is useful for program management, policy review, and research on rural development outcomes linked to RDPR implementation. The focus is on tracking the number of active workers over time to assess trends in demand for work and participation at the state level.",
  "generated_sector": "Rural; Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides an active thandapper list for villages of Kerala, supporting local revenue administration and record verification. It organizes village-level information alongside administrative references such as district and taluk, helping users locate relevant entries for governance, planning, and documentation workflows. The focus is on active listings rather than historical snapshots, making it suitable for operational use by departments and stakeholders working with land and revenue records in Kerala.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Union/State Government Administration"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together actual and estimated budget information for multiple years for organisations under the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY). It supports analysis of funding trends across communication and information technology initiatives, including comparisons between planned estimates and realized expenditures. Useful for budgeting review, policy monitoring, and transparency-focused research on how MeitY allocates resources in India.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Information and Technology"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Admin Boundary catalog provides administrative boundary information for Karnataka, supporting mapping, planning, and governance workflows. It covers hierarchical units such as districts, taluks, and village-level boundaries, enabling consistent spatial referencing across government and public services. The resources are useful for applications that require accurate administrative geographies, including service delivery planning and location-based analysis. Published under the Governance and Administration domain, it aligns with Union/State Government Administration needs.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Union/State Government Administration"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides advance estimates of Gross Domestic Product (GDP) for 2013-14 at factor cost, broken down by economic activity for Madhya Pradesh. It presents GDP values at both current prices and constant (2004-05) prices, enabling analysis of growth and structural changes across sectors. The estimates support timely economic assessment and planning by offering an early view of production outcomes before final accounts are released.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Macro Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together advance estimates of State income for Madhya Pradesh, published on a quarterly basis to provide an early indication of economic performance. These estimates are prepared shortly after the end of each quarter using information available at the time, and are subsequently scrutinized and revised in later preliminary and final estimates. The series supports timely monitoring of income trends and helps stakeholders assess short-term changes in the state economy.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Macro Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together DRDO-developed advanced demolition device products intended for national security and counter-terrorism and counter-insurgency operations. It covers technologies used to engage threats and mitigate risks, including remotely operated systems for hazardous tasks such as bomb detection and disposal. The collection is published by the Ministry of Defence and the Defence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO) and is relevant for defence preparedness and operational planning across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Defence; Para Military Forces"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles information on affiliated institutes associated with the Maharashtra State Board of Technical Education (MSBTE) for the 2025-26 academic period. It supports stakeholders in identifying MSBTE-linked polytechnic and technical education institutes, facilitating planning, admissions-related coordination, and institutional reference. The coverage is specific to Maharashtra, reflecting the state board’s jurisdiction and affiliation network.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Agricultural Technology Management Agency (ATMA) catalog supports dissemination and adoption of agricultural technologies through extension and research-linked activities. It focuses on improving farm practices and productivity by enabling knowledge transfer, capacity building, and technology management at the state level. The scope covers Karnataka, supporting stakeholders such as farmers, extension functionaries, and implementing agencies involved in agricultural research and extension. The catalog is intended to help users find ATMA-related information and resources for planning and implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Agricultural Research & Extension"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on agricultural workers and total workers in Punjab, supporting analysis of workforce composition and labour participation in the agricultural sector. It is useful for researchers, planners, and policymakers who need comparable worker indicators to understand employment patterns and inform agriculture and labour-related interventions. The focus is on Punjab, with data organized to help compare agricultural work against overall workforce totals.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Agricultural Marketing"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Agriculture Dealer License Report compiles statistical information from fertilizer and pesticide dealers’ licensing reports. It supports monitoring of licensed dealers and related compliance indicators for the fertilizer and pesticide supply chain. The catalog is intended for stakeholders who need aggregated views of dealer licensing trends and coverage to inform planning, oversight, and policy review. The geographic and temporal coverage are not specified in the provided scope information.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Fertilizers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Agriculture Department - PMKISAN catalog brings together district-wise information related to Pradhan Manthri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM-KISAN) for India. It supports tracking and verification of beneficiary-linked details and payments under the scheme, enabling analysis of coverage and distribution across districts. The catalog is intended for stakeholders who need scheme monitoring inputs for planning, reporting, and transparency around farmer income support. Data is organized as district-level details as on 27-09-2019.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Agricultural Produces"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Agriculture Inputs catalog focuses on information related to fertilizer input dealers in Karnataka. It supports tracking the availability and distribution of agriculture input supply through dealer counts, which can be used for planning, monitoring, and policy analysis in the fertilizer supply chain. The catalog is intended to help stakeholders understand market presence at the state level for better targeting of interventions and resource allocation.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Fertilizers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles agriculture land use statistics focusing on held land and cultivating account holders. It supports analysis of landholding patterns and the distribution of individuals or entities engaged in cultivation, useful for agricultural planning, policy monitoring, and research on rural livelihoods. The datasets are organized to help users compare land use and cultivation participation across the available time coverage. The publishing authority is not specified in the provided information.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Crops"
}

{
  "generated_description": "AgroStack Gadchiroli Maharashtra brings together information on farmers in Gadchiroli district of Maharashtra, focusing on land records and cropping patterns over the years. The catalog supports analysis of agricultural practices, including crop choices and fertilizer use, and can be used to study trends in organic farming adoption. It is intended to help stakeholders understand farm-level agricultural dynamics for planning, research, and targeted interventions in the region.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Crops, Organic farming"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles information on air-polluting industries in Punjab, covering units and categories across large, medium and small scale industrial establishments. It supports understanding of industry-wise air pollution sources and the classification of units, including categories associated with green and red designations. The included indicators are useful for environmental monitoring, planning air pollution control measures, and assessing the need for air pollution control devices. The focus aligns with Environment and Forest initiatives for pollution management.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Industrial Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers design and development of an Aircraft Mounted Accessory Gearbox (AMAGB) for the LIGHT COMBAT AIRCRAFT TEJAS. It focuses on a single-input, multi-output gearbox that transmits engine drive via a Power Take-Off (PTO) shaft at rated speed of 16,810 rpm to power multiple aircraft accessories. The work supports defence aviation systems by enabling reliable transmission of power for onboard functions such as generator and starter operations. It is undertaken in India by DRDO through CVRDE under the Ministry of Defence.",
  "generated_sector": "Defence; Air Force"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog lists Akshaya Centres (Common Service Centres) in Kerala, supporting the district-wide e-literacy initiative for mass transformation of ICT. It helps users locate citizen-facing service points that provide e-governance services and related support. The information is useful for planning, outreach, and service delivery by enabling access to CSC/Akshaya infrastructure across Kerala.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Local Government Administration"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Satellite-derived ocean albedo products generated from Oceansat-2 Ocean Color Monitor (OCM) support studies of surface energy balance, mid- to long-term weather prediction, and global climate change research. The catalog provides a value-added parameter derived from OCM observations across multiple VNIR spectral bands, enabling analysis of ocean surface reflectance over India. Published by the Department of Space, Indian Space Research Organization, and National Remote Sensing Centre, the resources are suited for remote sensing research and climate-related applications.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Ecology"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles information on all art educational institutions in Tamil Nadu, supporting discovery of institutions offering art-focused education. It is useful for students, parents, researchers, and education planners seeking to map availability of art training and related academic programs within the state. The collection aligns with the Art and Culture domain and can support directory-style use cases such as outreach, admissions planning, and comparative study of art education infrastructure across Tamil Nadu.",
  "generated_sector": "Art and Culture; Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The All India Advocate List provides district-wise information on enrolled advocates across India, including enrollment number, name, address, and date of enrollment. It supports legal administration, verification and reference of advocate credentials, and helps stakeholders maintain up-to-date records for professional practice. Published by the Ministry of Law and Justice, Department of Legal Affairs, the catalog is organized to enable searching and use of advocate enrollment details at the district level throughout India.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Union/State Government Administration, Judiciary; District Court"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles All India Index Numbers of Wholesale Prices for Punjab, supporting analysis of price movements across food, fuel, minerals, power, and manufactured products. It is useful for researchers, policymakers, and businesses tracking inflation trends and commodity-specific cost changes. The index series helps compare wholesale price dynamics over time for broad product groups, including both food and non-food articles.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Prices"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Annual allocation and fund release data under the Backward Region Grant Fund (BRGF) are compiled for India. The BRGF programme, implemented by the Ministry of Panchayati Raj, supports identified backward districts to address regional development imbalances through Development Grant and Capacity Building windows. The catalog enables tracking of district-level financial flows over time, supporting monitoring, planning, and evaluation of grant utilization across States.",
  "generated_sector": "Rural; Panchayati Raj"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers district-wise allocation of funds under the Special Area Development Programme (SADP) in Tamil Nadu from 2016-17 to 2019-20. It brings together allocation information across government departments to support tracking of programme funding, planning, and monitoring of special area development initiatives. The focus is on how SADP resources are distributed within Tamil Nadu over the specified financial years, enabling comparative analysis across districts and time.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Union/State Government Administration"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers district-wise allocation of funds under the State Balance Growth Fund (SBGF) in Tamil Nadu from 2013-14 to 2019-20. It compiles allocations across multiple indicators to support analysis of how SBGF resources are distributed over time within the state. These data are useful for government planning, monitoring fund flows, and evaluating regional allocation patterns. The focus aligns with Union/State Government Administration functions related to state-level financial transfers.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Union/State Government Administration"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides location-wise daily ambient air quality data for Odisha, covering key pollutants such as Sulfur dioxide, Nitrogen dioxide, Respirable Suspended Particulate Matter (RSPM) and Suspended Particulate Matter (SPM). It supports monitoring and analysis of air quality trends across stations, including changes in station availability over time due to shifts, closures, or relocation against NAMP monitoring guidelines. The datasets are useful for environmental assessment, compliance-oriented studies, and public health and policy planning related to industrial and traffic-related air pollution.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Industrial Air Pollution, Environment and Forest; Vehicular Air Pollution, Environment and Forest; Residential Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together ambulance details for Maharashtra, focused on District Nagpur. It supports access to information relevant to emergency medical transport, helping users locate and understand ambulance availability and related service details at the district level. The emphasis on ambulance operations aligns with health service planning and public awareness for faster response during medical emergencies.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles information on the amount of grants and loans disbursed to various village industries in Punjab by the Khadi & Village Industries Board. It supports tracking financial assistance flows and assessing funding levels across different village industry activities. The data is useful for monitoring program implementation, planning future disbursements, and conducting reviews of how support is distributed within Punjab’s village industries.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Cottage"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together student enrolment information for municipal schools in Amravati city, covering 63 schools across all five administrative zones and three mediums of instruction. It supports analysis of enrolment patterns by school and instructional medium, useful for education planning, resource allocation, and monitoring access at the local level. The data is published by the Education Department of Amravati Municipal Corporation and focuses on school-level student counts for elementary and secondary education.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles information on Anganawadi Centres with tap water supply under the JJM in Karnataka. It supports monitoring of water access for early childhood care and education facilities, helping planners and administrators assess coverage and service delivery. The focus is on rural development-linked water provisioning for Anganawadi centres, aligning with JJM implementation and reporting needs under RDPR.",
  "generated_sector": "Rural; Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together animal husbandry and dairying statistics for Gujarat, covering key production indicators such as milk and wool, along with allied infrastructure and facilities supporting dairying activities. It is useful for planning, monitoring and analysis by stakeholders interested in livestock-based livelihoods and dairy value chains. The focus on Gujarat enables state-level assessment of trends in animal husbandry and dairy development.",
  "generated_sector": "Animal Husbandry; Dairying"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Annual budget documents for DRDO outline how funds are assessed, prioritized, and allocated across technology clusters. They cover the preparation of overall DRDO budget estimates, including Revised Budget Estimates (RE) based on expenditure review, and Forecast Budget Estimates (FBE) for the next financial year. The focus is on enhancing allocations for labs/establishments, programmes, and high-value projects. Published under the Ministry of Defence and the Defence Research and Development Organisation, the budget information applies across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Defence; Army"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides annual Building Construction Cost index data for Punjab, supporting tracking of changes in construction costs over time. It is useful for budgeting, cost estimation, and planning by stakeholders who need to adjust for movements in labour, material, and wage-related components. The focus on an index format helps compare cost trends across years for construction activities in Punjab. Published as part of official statistics on construction cost dynamics.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Prices"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides the Annual Construction Cost Index for Punjab state, capturing changes in building construction costs over time. It supports analysis of cost movements driven by labour, materials, and wages, helping stakeholders plan budgets, estimate project escalation, and compare construction cost trends. The focus is on construction cost indexing for Punjab, enabling use in procurement, contract management, and policy and planning related to the construction sector.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Prices"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Annual estimates for Gujarat covering Gross State Domestic Product (GSDP), Net State Domestic Product (NSDP) and NSDP per capita income. The series is provided at current prices and at constant prices with base year 2011-12, supporting analysis of growth trends and changes in income levels over time. Published as quick annual estimates, it is useful for state economic planning, policy evaluation, and comparative macroeconomic studies within Gujarat.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Macro Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides annual expenditure data comparing Total Plan and Non-Plan outlays with the figures from the last two years, supporting budget monitoring and trend analysis. It covers the period from 2017-18 to 2020-21 and focuses on Karnataka. The resources are useful for assessing how planned versus non-planned spending evolves over time and for informing infrastructure-related financial planning and review.",
  "generated_sector": "Infrastructure; Roads"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides district-level rainfall position data for Madhya Pradesh, covering monsoon season months of June, July, August and September. It includes actual rainfall and normal rainfall (long-term average) along with the percentage deviation of rainfall from normal for each district. Annual resources support year-wise analysis of rainfall patterns and deviations, useful for agriculture planning, drought/forecast assessments, and monitoring monsoon performance in Madhya Pradesh.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Crops"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Annual Survey of Industries Results of Gujarat compiles industry statistics for Gujarat, covering factories and persons engaged. It presents key economic indicators such as fixed capital, total output values, gross value added and net value added, reported in Rs. crore. The catalog supports analysis of manufacturing activity, productivity and value creation, and can be used for planning, research and policy evaluation by stakeholders interested in Gujarat’s industrial performance. Published as part of the Annual Survey of Industries program.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Manufacturing"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles annual information on forest planting of major tree species in Punjab, covering species such as eucalyptus, shisham, kikar, khair, mulberry, chil and other miscellaneous varieties. It supports monitoring of afforestation activities and planning for species-specific forestry interventions. The focus on annual planting makes it useful for tracking trends over time and informing forest management decisions in Punjab. Published under the Environment and Forest domain.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles annual records of patients treated in the Out Patient Department (OPD) and Indoor Patient Department (IPD) at the National Institute of Homoeopathy (NIH), Kolkata. It supports analysis of patient flow and service utilization across OPD and IPD over time, useful for monitoring demand, planning capacity, and informing healthcare management within the institute. Published by the Ministry of AYUSH through the National Institute of Homoeopathy (NIH). The geographic coverage is India, with records specific to NIH, Kolkata.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Annual records of radiology, ultrasonography, ECG and PFT investigations conducted at NIH Hospital support clinical diagnosis, monitoring of patient response to homoeopathic treatment, and prognosis decisions. The catalog covers counts of key diagnostic tests including X-ray, Ultrasound (USG), Hysterosalpingography (HSG), Electrocardiography (ECG), Holter ECG, and Pulmonary Function Test (PFT). Published by the Ministry of AYUSH under the National Institute of Homoeopathy (NIH), the data reflects investigation activity at NIH Hospital.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles an annual record of scientific articles published from the National Institute of Homoeopathy (NIH) under the Ministry of AYUSH. It covers publications by NIH faculties and doctors, including research papers, published seminar abstracts in research medical journals, and related cured clinical cases. The focus is on health research outputs produced by NIH, supporting tracking of scholarly activity and evidence generation over time.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides an annual record of surgeries performed at the National Institute of Homoeopathy (NIH) under the Department of Surgery. It covers counts of procedures across General Surgery, Lower Segment Caesarean Section (LSCS), Gynaecology, Orthopaedics, and Eye. The data supports monitoring surgical service delivery within an AYUSH homoeopathic care setting, including cases where patients receive homoeopathic treatment before and after surgery. The geographic coverage is at NIH, with records organized by year.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles application-wise counts of documents along with stamp duty and registration fees collected under the registration process. It supports analysis of transaction volumes and fee patterns for revenue administration and policy monitoring. The focus is on Maharashtra, enabling comparisons across applications and related fee components. Data are organized to help stakeholders assess demand for registration services and understand how stamp duty and registration fees contribute to revenue.",
  "generated_sector": "Revenue; Macro Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles district-wise statistics on area irrigated by different sources of irrigation in Tamil Nadu, under the SCR (Seasons Crop Report) series. It covers the editions 2016-17, 2017-18, and 2018-19, enabling comparison of irrigation source-wise coverage across districts within the City of SCR, Tamil Nadu. Useful for agricultural planning, irrigation management, and monitoring changes in irrigated area over successive SCR reporting years.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Irrigation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles district-level statistics on the area under high yielding and local varieties of principal cereals in Tamil Nadu, drawing from the Season and Crop Report (SCR). It covers the editions 2016-17, 2017-18, and 2018-19, enabling year-wise comparison of crop area across districts. The focus on principal cereals supports agricultural planning, monitoring of varietal adoption, and analysis of seasonal crop patterns for Tamil Nadu.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Crops"
